# Prompt improvement — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Recursive prompt workflow powered by [ri-engine](https://github.com/russfranky/recursive-intelligence).

## Quick commands

```bash
# One-time setup (already done if you ran integrate init)
ri-engine integrate init

# Improve + approve to runbook (recommended each canon change)
ri-engine integrate improve

# Start over — preview then confirm
ri-engine integrate reset
ri-engine integrate reset --yes
ri-engine integrate reset --yes --reinit   # reset + fresh init

# Check integration status
ri-engine integrate status
```

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `prompts/seed/{{AGENT_SLUG}}.md` | Hand-written canon + anti-patterns |
| `{{CONFIG_PATH}}` | VSR config |
| `runbook/RUNBOOK.md` | **Agents start here** |
| `.ri-engine/project.yaml` | Integration manifest |

## Recursive loop

1. Edit seed (canon / anti-patterns) when agents fail a new way
2. `ri-engine integrate improve` → VSR until plateau → runbook
3. **Hand-merge** domain rules into `runbook/prompts/{{AGENT_SLUG}}.md` if output is generic
4. Point Cursor / Claude Code at `runbook/RUNBOOK.md`

High rubric fitness can still be generic — see [integration_patterns.md](https://github.com/russfranky/recursive-intelligence/blob/main/docs/integration_patterns.md).

## Optional

